        <body>
            <div xml:id="d484">

                <pb facs="0520" n="486" sameAs="frus:frus1897/pg486"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Woodford to Mr. Sherman.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1897-12-04"><hi rendition="#italic">December 4, 1897</hi></date>.
                        (Received Dec. 18.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 88.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to my dispatch No. 82, of
                    November 29, 1897, and my cable of November 28, 1897, I have the honor to inform
                    you that, confirming the information therein conveyed, I received yesterday a
                    formal and courteous note from the Spanish minister of state, stating that the
                    American citizen Luis Someillan had been released from prison, and that no
                    citizen of the United States now remained imprisoned in the Island of Cuba. I
                    have acknowledged the receipt of the note. I inclose herein a copy of the note,
                    with translation.</p>
                <p>I have the honor, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Stewart L.
                    Woodford.</hi></signed></closer>



                <xi:include href="d484-a1.xml" xpointer="d484-a1"/>
